      {
        "id": "lem-finite-dimensional-galerkin-minmax",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "title": "Finite-dimensional conforming Ritz values satisfy min–max",
        "dependency_level": 0,
        "deps": [
          "def-bounded-coercive-and-symmetric-sesquilinear-forms",
          "def-bounded-linear-operator",
          "def-compact-linear-operator",
          "def-countable-choice",
          "cor-finite-dimensional-inner-product-spaces-have-orthonormal-bases",
          "cor-finite-dimensional-normed-spaces-are-banach",
          "def-hilbert-space",
          "def-real-and-complex-inner-product-space",
          "thm-extreme-value-metric",
          "thm-heine-borel-rn",
          "thm-rank-nullity",
          "thm-spectral-theorem-for-compact-self-adjoint-operators"
        ],
        "statement": "Assume Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $V_h$ be an\n$N$-dimensional subspace of a real or complex Hilbert space $V$, with\n$N\\ge1$. Let $a$ be a bounded Hermitian coercive form on $V$ and let\n$b(u,v):=(Ju,Jv)_H$ for a bounded injective linear map $J:V\\to H$ into a\nHilbert space. The generalized Ritz problem on $V_h$ is\n$$a(u_h,v_h)=\\lambda_h b(u_h,v_h)\\qquad(v_h\\in V_h).$$\nIts eigenvalues, listed with multiplicity in increasing order, are positive\nnumbers $\\lambda_{h,1}\\le\\cdots\\le\\lambda_{h,N}$. For every\n$1\\le m\\le N$,\n$$\\lambda_{h,m}=\\min_{\\substack{W_h\\subseteq V_h\\\\\\dim W_h=m}} \\max_{v_h\\in W_h\\setminus\\{0\\}} \\frac{a(v_h,v_h)}{b(v_h,v_h)}.$$\n\n"
      },
